text:
Jordan: quick heads-up — ran into a confusing error shape in the node sdk when token refresh fails. user sees 500 + 'internal error' with no retry hint. cc @Maeve
Maeve: yikes. do we have a mapping table for auth -> 401/403 vs transient 5xx?
Jordan: we do in the api docs but SDKs aren't consistent. python maps refresh failure to AuthError, node just throws generic Error.
Liam: that's a regression from last parity pass. node used to surface typed errors. probably slipped in the rewrite.
Priya: hmm onboarding feedback: customers complain the message "internal error" makes them call support. we should provide actionable text + retry hint in the exception.
Eli: agree. suggestion: typed exceptions + structured fields: ``type``, ``status_code``, ``should_retry``, ``retry_after``. sample: ``AuthError { message, status_code: 401, should_retry: false }``
Maeve: love structured fields. also add a short human-friendly summary and a machine field for programmatic checks. e.g., ``summary: 'invalid api key'`` + ``code: 'auth.invalid_key'``
Jordan: +1. can we standardize names across SDKs? propose names: AuthError, RateLimitError, ServiceUnavailableError, ValidationError, InternalServerError
Liam: small ask: map HTTP 429 -> RateLimitError and include parsed ``Retry-After`` if present. for 5xx, default to InternalServerError with ``should_retry: true`` unless we detect deterministic failure.
Priya: operationally we need docs + examples in quickstart. sample app should show how to catch and branch on typed errors instead of string matching. small snippet idea:
Priya: ```js
try {
  await client.generate(prompt)
} catch (err) {
  if (err instanceof RateLimitError) {
    // surface backoff UI
  } else if (err instanceof AuthError) {
    // show reauth flow
  } else if (err.should_retry) {
    // retry with jitter
  } else {
    throw err
  }
}
```
Eli: does gap analysis: node, python, go, java. i can make a matrix of current thrown types vs desired types and submit a PR.
Maeve: awesome. can we also normalize error_message content length? avoid stack dumps in message field — put stack in ``debug_info`` only. customers shouldn't see internal traces in user-facing messages. :no_entry_sign:
Jordan: +1 — important for privacy/compliance. Also add telemetry tag so SRE can map error incidences to SDK versions.
devex-bot: reminder — create a small issue for SDK parity and link to the matrix. use label "sdk-errors" and assign to @Eli.
Eli: I'll open the issue with proposed schema, mapping matrix, and sample quickstart patch today. putting a draft PR in the devex repo for review.
Liam: once PR lands, can we do a canary release for node and python and validate with a small user test? we should track error shapes in logs for 48h.
Priya: i'll add a quickstart checklist item: update sample app, docs note about message shapes, and a migration note for vNext. also will update onboarding FAQ to cover common auth/rl issues.
Jordan: thanks all — action items: Eli issue + PR, Maeve doc blurb, Priya onboarding updates, Liam canary plan. ping me if you need help. :thumbsup:
Maeve: will write the tiny doc snippet and add examples for parsing errors in TS.
Eli: filed https://github.com/redwood-inference/devex/issues/1423 (draft) — includes proposed schema and per-sdk matrix. feedback welcome.
Jordan: perfect, closing the loop. we'll track in the SDK errors epic.
